# A store into an own Array's element takes the conversion edge of a value of another number type, as a write through
# a path does (OPUS-PATHCONV-20260929-10): `a[1]: z` gives an int to a size_t element, and this program has no receiver
# row.  Before, the store had no edge and no refusal: C converted.
fn: m () size_t
    int: z 5
    []: size_t a 2
    a[1]: z
    return: a[1]

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
